Phase 2 (FullSpectrum Local-Z, LZ1+LZ2): introduce the Local-Z planner
state types in Print.hpp.

Three additions (combines two task units LZ1 + LZ2 since both touch
the same file):

1. `struct LocalZInterval` — describes one source layer's Local-Z plan:
   layer_id, z_lo / z_hi span, base_height, sublayer_height,
   has_mixed_paint flag, plus an index range into the PrintObject's
   m_local_z_sublayer_plan vector for the SubLayerPlan entries.

2. `struct SubLayerPlan` — one sub-slice of a Local-Z interval.
   Carries per-extruder XY masks (painted_masks_by_extruder), the
   fixed-pattern masks (fixed_painted_masks_by_extruder for manual
   pattern entries that mustn't be redistributed by cadence),
   base_masks for unpainted regions, and dependency_group +
   dependency_order for LocalZOrderOptimizer (patch 0023) to use
   when sorting sublayers within a group.

3. `PrintObject` accessors + private members:
   - `local_z_intervals()` / `local_z_sublayer_plan()` getters
   - `set_local_z_plan(intervals, sublayers)` mutator
   - `clear_local_z_plan()` reset
   - `m_local_z_intervals` + `m_local_z_sublayer_plan` private storage

4. `WipeTowerData::local_z_tool_changes` — per-layer Local-Z purge
   toolchange sequences, populated by patches 0046+ (WipeTower2
   plan_local_z_toolchange). Indexed parallel to `tool_changes`;
   inner vectors hold the purge passes that fire between adjacent
   sublayers within one source layer's Local-Z interval. Empty for
   non-Local-Z layers. Cleared in `WipeTowerData::clear()`.

DEAD CODE in isolation: nothing reads from any of these fields yet.
The PrintObjectSlice.cpp planner (patch 0045) populates them; the
GCode.cpp Z-walk emitter (patch 0048) consumes them. Until those
land, this patch is structural scaffolding that survives every slice
unchanged.

Ported semantically from FS v0.9.9
(`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit b3c41fda),
`src/libslic3r/Print.hpp` lines 57-88 (struct definitions),
431-442 (accessors), 591-593 (members), 777, 791 (WipeTowerData).
Snapmaker fork pre-introduced LocalZInterval + SubLayerPlan; OrcaXR's
v2.3.2 base has neither, so this patch is technically a merge of the
Snapmaker scaffolding + the FS additions (dependency_group/_order +
fixed_painted_masks_by_extruder).

